## Claim 6 — ruled: accepted residue, not a W-041 defect
- At 682e6f8 (the generator commit), running build.sh twice leaves the tree
  clean, so the page was exact for its own tree. At bc53139, build.sh dirties
  backlog-body.html and bisellium-backlog.html (the W-041 row only). The
  bookkeeping commit (verify + handoff) moved the officina after generation.
- Regenerating inside the bookkeeping commit would still not capture
  review/done, which are written after it. After merge, trunk will show W-041
  as `building` until something regenerates the page.
- The brief puts staleness out of scope and names the checkpoint's build.sh as
  the regeneration point ("A check rule for page staleness" — Out of scope).
  That is where honesty lands. The orchestrator MUST run build.sh at the
  post-merge checkpoint. Until then the trunk page shows one done opus as
  building.
- Instance or class: this is an instance. searched: every writeFileSync in
  scripts/*.mjs and docs/design/dossier/*.mjs, plus build.sh. backlog-page.mjs
  is the only committed artifact generated from per-opus bookkeeping.
  progress-body.html and body.html are hand-written, so they go stale the way
  prose does (the handoff itself notes "progress page still owes rows for
  cascades 23–24"), not through a generator. build-arch.mjs reads docs/*.md.
  The structural cousin is scripts/changelog.mjs → CHANGELOG.md, which cannot
  contain its own commit either. That is the same accepted shape.

